  "root_rationale": [
    "The source universally asserts an exact formula for all n>=4. A bound a(11)<=57<58 is a complete refutation, not a proved parameter subcase of a still-open universal assertion.",
    "n=11 is an interior index beyond the displayed data, not an excluded first-index/domain correction. The construction respects connectedness, holes and translation-only placement.",
    "The review explicitly finds that the classical tree-center construction gives61 and the inspected older free-piece and embedding constructions do not yield57. No complete same-object routine-corollary bridge has been established.",
    "Standard enumeration and optimization receive no credit. Their use does not alone classify the resulting full counterexample as a known theorem or routine corollary. Requiring a scalable family, exact optimum or new algorithm would add a requirement absent from the source and not applied to earlier accepted individual counterexamples.",
    "This remains a borderline judgment about substantive scope. Formal proof size, sunk effort, and the campaign target are not evidence for eligibility. No new structural theorem or global priority is asserted."
  ],
  "standing_dissent": "Recent registry extrapolation, one-cell improvement at one finite index, established search methods and punctured diamonds; no optimum or general law. Reviewer recommends exclusion on precisely this basis. Preserve in final review and acceptance deliberation.",
